16116e46"}, "tests/test_totals.py": {"bytes": 443, "mtime": 1791845574.1071954, "sha256": "b33548e48cc53a932d7b6ef1355d7ed4c9b018e02cf492672becf8853777a1c3"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/a95d432f7bc115e3b642c41ee48344d81c6221c7/omp", "-p", "`tests/test_totals.py` is failing. Fix the bug.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-cap30-19-off/omp-19/transcripts/with/trig-omp-multistep/5/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-cap30-19-off/omp-19/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/5/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/a95d432f7bc115e3b642c41ee48344d81c6221c7/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates binary-float products (`19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `1998`). Fix it at the conversion boundary using exact decimal arithmetic.\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, in `to_cents`, not in the totals code. It did `int(amount * 100)`, and `int()` cuts off the decimal part. Prices like 19.99 can't be stored exactly as floats, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.999\u2026` and became 1998 cents instead of 1999. The same thing happened to 0.29 and 4.35, so every total built on them was off by a cent.\n\n**Change (`ledger/currency.py`, `to_cents`):** the amount is now converted with `Decimal(str(amount))`, which keeps the price exactly as it's written (19.99 stays 19.99). It is then multiplied by 100 and rounded half up to whole cents. The rest of the code already works in integer cents, so nothing else needed changing.\n\n**Checks:**\n- pytest isn't installed for the system `python3`, so I put it in a temporary venv at `/tmp/v` and ran `/tmp/v/bin/python -m pytest tests -q`: all 5 tests pass, the 4 in `test_totals.py` and 1 in `test_report.py`.\n- I ran every amount from 0.00 to 9999.99 through `to_cents(c/100)` and every one came back as exactly `c` cents. Before the fix, many of them were one cent short.\n- Spot checks: `-19.99` gives -1999, the string `\"2.50\"` gives 250, the integer `3` gives 300.\n\n**Behaviour changes:**\n- Amounts finer than a cent now round half up instead of being cut off: `1.005` becomes 101, where before it became 100. That fits \"rounding half up\" in `discounts.py`, but it is a change if anything relied on the old cut-off.\n- Halves round away from zero for negative amounts, so -1.005 becomes -101.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 47074, "requests_cache_write": 14726, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1198448, "requests_count": 4, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 1838, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 9, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:51:32.297439+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.306, "t_checker_s": 0.4, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "toke